Subject: [PATCH 4/5] proto(sound): constant-level shortcut for the SSG
 per-channel outputs

Variant (c) of the YM decimator prototype: a channel whose whole window of
fed levels holds one value writes that value instead of the FIR output
(generalizes the silent-channel skip). In double the FIR of a constant
differs from the level by at most 1.2e-15 (rounding of v x sum(c)); after
the cast to the card's float rows the result is the same for every YM2149
level at every output instant and design (DecimatorDot_Test), and for 4.1M
random levels (DISABLED_ConstantWindowStatistics: 0 mismatches). Quality
harness A/B: all renders identical.

Prototype, docs/inprogress/2026-10-03-zx-multisound/ym-decimator-prototype.md
